---
description: graphify knowledge graph context
alwaysApply: true
---
Use Graphify first when a project already has `graphify-out/graph.json`:
- `graphify query "<question>"` for codebase and architecture questions.
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` for dependency paths.
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` for related nodes.
Use Read, Grep, Glob, or shell search directly when Graphify has oriented the task and exact lines are needed, or when the project has no graph yet.
After modifying code in a graph-enabled project, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current.
